<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Apple's privacy manifest, required since 2024 for any "required reason
	API" usage – see https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/privacy_manifest_files/describing_use_of_required_reason_api.
	Audited by grepping the whole app for every required-reason API category
	Apple defines (UserDefaults, file timestamps, system boot time, disk
	space, active keyboard): only UserDefaults/@AppStorage turned up (FTP,
	Max/Resting Heart Rate, Heart Rate Zone boundaries, the language
	override, Vibration/Interval Sound, the last-used mode/target values, …
	– all app-scoped settings, see SettingsView/WorkoutSession/ControlView/
	LanguageManager/TrainerConnection/BluetoothManager/RouteStore/
	WorkoutProgramStore). No App Group, no extension, no widget shares any
	of it with another app – reason CA92.1 ("access user defaults to read
	and write information that is only accessible to the app itself") is
	the exact fit; 1C8F.1 (its sibling reason, for App-Group-shared
	UserDefaults) does not apply here.

	This app has zero third-party SDKs, so there is nothing here whose own
	privacy manifest would need aggregating, and no collected-data-types
	declaration to fold in from elsewhere. `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes` is
	deliberately omitted rather than guessed at – it exists mainly to feed
	that SDK-aggregation process (and to mirror it for documentation), not
	as a build-time requirement, and the actual, mandatory data-collection
	disclosure (Health & Fitness data via HealthKit, Bluetooth device data)
	belongs in App Store Connect's separate "App Privacy" questionnaire, a
	web-based step this file doesn't substitute for.

	No tracking, ever: no ads, no analytics, no cross-app/cross-site
	identifiers, nothing phoned home to a tracking domain.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
